Hi,

Does anyone know why the Elf has a default alignment, at the quest start, of
Chaotic?
I got a hold of the WCST Nethack Spoilers file (V7.0) and it listed the Elf
as being Lawful. (Yeah, I know it's out of date with NH 3.1.1 - which I'm
using)
In keeping with Tolkien's elves, and the general idea of elves in mythology
was that they were the good guys. Totally against evil.

From the point of view of Artifacts, you have to be VERY carefully what you
ask for if your given a wish. I started the game and found lying next to me
a wand of wishing. Brilliant! I asked for the "blessed +3 gray dragon scale
mail" - got it. Put it on.
Then I asked for "blessed +3 long sword named Excalibur", got it. It blew up
in my face and killed me! Why? Because it has a Lawful alignment and I was a
chaotic character. A prize of the daftest death? :-)

I think it's out of line that an elf cannot use, and I quote the code:

"Orcrist",            ELVEN_BROADSWORD,
or
"Sting",          ELVEN_DAGGER,

They're both lawful, and both elven. After my experience of Excalibur I'm
keeping my paws well away from these 2!

BTW, if I was to change my alignment, I have to change god, right? So would
my quest be different?

Also, if your Neutral, will Lawful or Chaotic artifacts still kill you, or
try to jump out of your hands?

